Vehicle electrification: Electric vehicles and their charging infrastructure require components that support reliable electrical performance and electromagnetic compatibility.
Regulatory and safety requirements: Electromagnetic compatibility standards encourage manufacturers to incorporate suitable suppression components into electronic designs.
Electronic Components & Electromagnetic Compatibility Watch
Suppression ceramic capacitors are important components in electronic systems where electrical noise must be controlled to maintain reliable operation. These capacitors help limit unwanted interference in power supplies, consumer electronics, industrial equipment, automotive electronics and communication systems.
The growing use of power electronics in electric vehicles, charging equipment and connected devices is increasing the importance of reliable EMI and RFI suppression. X-class capacitors are generally used for line-to-line interference suppression, while Y-class capacitors are designed for line-to-ground applications subject to specific safety requirements.
Manufacturers are focusing on component reliability, electrical performance, compact designs and compliance with applicable safety standards. However, competition, raw material costs, manufacturing quality requirements and the need for rigorous certification can influence product development and purchasing decisions. Suppliers must balance performance, cost and reliability to meet the requirements of increasingly sophisticated electronic systems.
